      <Quiz id="quiz-queue" questions={quiz} />
      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Queue: first in, first out. Enqueue at the rear, dequeue at the front.</li>
          <li><code>dequeue</code> removes and returns the front item; <code>peek</code> only looks.</li>
          <li>In <code>LinkedQueue</code>, <code>enqueue</code> links the old rear to the new node first, then moves <code>rear</code>.</li>
          <li>When the last node leaves, both <code>front</code> and <code>rear</code> become <code>null</code>.</li>
          <li>LIFO and FIFO are rules. Arrays and linked lists are storage. Any rule can use either.</li>
        </ol>
